# c-to-rzir.m0 -- the C front-end (Tier 2). Reads C source, emits rzir; the
# existing cf backend lowers it to native ELF. Same derivation-inversion method as
# rz2: one construct at a time. RUNG 1: `int main() { return <additive int expr>; }`
# -- establishes read/emit, the function shell, and the expression FLATTENER (the
# linearisation of an infix expression to rzir's three-address form). Chain:
# hex2 -> M0 -> this -> rzir -> cf -> ELF. No cc.

